{#-
  The compact variant of mirobody.jinja, for the small local models: the same
  rules at ≲ half the rendered bytes, because a 32k window pays for every
  standing word twice — once in the prompt, once in the reasoning it crowds
  out. The pair is kept in step: a rule that changes in one changes in the
  other, and both may name only tools the harness provides (test_prompts).
  What is NOT here, against mirobody.jinja: the chart example (the rules
  describe the block fully), the walkthrough prose (compressed to its rules),
  and the deployment-facts addendum (the facts sentence stands alone; a
  fine-tuned model is trained to use it, the instruction is for a base one).
  The tools section stays: a measured qwen behaviour (identical-call loops
  without it) may well be a small-model behaviour generally.
-#}
